Subject: [PATCH] application: bound shutdown so Exit always ends Kodi

A Python service add-on that does not check abortRequested (seen with
plugin.service.emby-next-gen 12.4.24) blocks CScriptInvocationManager::
Uninitialize() in std::thread::join() forever. A player that waits on a
stalled network source (the same add-on's local proxy) blocks
ClosePlayer() for a minute or more. On LibreELEC systemd kills Kodi after
a timeout; as a desktop session Kodi stays on screen.
When Stop() starts, allow the shutdown 30 seconds, then _Exit with the
normal exit code.

--- a/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/application/Application.cpp
@@ -179,8 +179,10 @@
 #include <chrono>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <memory>
 #include <mutex>
+#include <thread>
 
 #include <tinyxml.h>
 
@@ -1829,6 +1831,20 @@
 
   CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Stopping the application...");
 
+  // Stop() and Cleanup() can block forever: a Python service add-on that ignores
+  // abortRequested blocks CScriptInvocationManager::Uninitialize() in thread::join(), and
+  // a player that waits on a stalled network source blocks ClosePlayer(). As a desktop
+  // session Kodi then stays on screen. Give the shutdown 30 seconds, then exit anyway.
+  std::thread(
+      [exitCode]
+      {
+        std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::seconds(30));
+        CLog::Log(LOGWARNING, "Shutdown did not finish in 30 seconds; exiting with code {}",
+                  exitCode);
+        std::_Exit(exitCode);
+      })
+      .detach();
+
   bool success = true;
 
   CLog::Log(LOGINFO, "Stopping player");
